EXT. DRIVE-IN THEATER PARKING FIELD - NIGHT

A gravel lot under a weathered screen. Speaker posts stand in rows like headstones. The movie plays silent; the glow washes across a dozen parked cars.

Four teenagers sit on the hood of a rusted pickup. JAMAL "JAY" WHITFIELD (17, varsity jacket, restless) tosses a bottle cap. His best friend LENORE "NORI" VASQUEZ-HALL (17, band tee, headphones around her neck) swings her legs. ARCHIE PLUMMER (16, braces, thick glasses) peels a sticker off a soda can. Beside them, SABRINA DOYLE (17, thrift-store dress, a camera on a strap) frames shots of the screen.

JAY
Ten bucks says he kisses her.

NORI
He doesn't kiss her. He dies in act three.

ARCHIE
He doesn't die.

NORI
He dies, Archie.

ARCHIE
You've seen it?

NORI
Twice.

JAY
Then why'd we come?

NORI
Because it's summer and nobody has a car that works.

GIRL WITH CAMERA
Hold still, Jay. Your jacket's glowing blue.

JAY
Sabrina, I'm not posing.

SABRINA
It looks nice.

JAY
Does it?

NORI
Archie, are you eating the whole bag?

ARCHIE
It's a family bag.

NORI
We're a family?

JAY
We're the closest thing Archie's got.

ARCHIE
That's not funny.

SABRINA
It's a little funny.

ARCHIE
Okay, a little.

JAY
So what's after this? College? Real life?

NORI
Next September.

SABRINA
Don't say it like that.

NORI
Like what?

SABRINA
Like it's a funeral.

ARCHIE
I'm going to Ohio.

JAY
Ohio?

ARCHIE
They have a good robotics program.

NORI
Ohio. Wow.

JAY
You'll be great, Arch.

ARCHIE
Will I?

JAY
You'll be the best.

SABRINA
I'm staying here. Dad's shop.

JAY
You hate the shop.

SABRINA
I like the darkroom.

NORI
Then take pictures of it.

SABRINA
I will.

She raises the camera and fires. The shutter clicks. In the frame, three faces glow blue in the screen light, and one of them, Jay's, looks away.

JAY
What about me?

NORI
What about you?

JAY
Where do I go?

NORI
Anywhere, Jay.

ARCHIE
Somewhere with better snacks.

They laugh. On the screen, the hero delivers his last line without sound. Nori mouths along. Jay hurls the bottle cap at the screen. It pings off the post.

JAY
Nobody ever remembers the summer, they remember the end of it.

SABRINA
(quietly)
Then let's make it a long one.
